   "end_time": null,
   "all_day": false,
   "description": "A new project from Piper Burns, longtime music and worrying enthusiast. Unrelenting Fear is a fresh batch of Piper\u2019s prehistoric caveman rock music covering such topics as : Meat, Gravy, Work, Online Shopping, Being Annoyed, Being Annoying, Eating Dog Food, Shipwrecks, long lost friends and the Unrelenting Fear that comes with each new day. For those who recall Piper\u2019s old band, The Steves, these new songs will have a familiar place in your auditory experience as well as some familiar faces for the live band! Featuring longtime friends and collaborators, Chris Sleightholm (Snake River) Neil Lutz (Black Thunder) Andy Beisel (Wolf Willow) and Pearl Bogdan (The Steves). This show will be celebrating the release of a tape cassette, featuring the previously mentioned music.\n\nDoors at 8pm, Show at 10pm.",
